    "summary": "Model built and all L1/L2/L3 checks passed.\n\nRoot cause of the earlier failure: the instance's girder count (girder.count_per_span = 3) was not actually present in the layer the formula resolver reads, so at generate_model time the L2-1 recompute evaluated MR-02 with a default n_girders = 4 and MR-04 with count = 8. Those recomputed girder.A/I and bearing counts disagreed with the accepted decisions (which had correctly used 3 girders), failing the check. Repair: re-wrote the instance with girder.count_per_span = 3; the formulas then resolved n_girders = 3 and count = 6, matching every accepted decision. Re-ran the modal analysis (f1 unchanged) and regenerated successfully.\n\nModel (spine_beam_2d, simply supported, single 30 m span):\n- Girder: 3 precast prestressed small-box girders, C40 (Ec = 32500 MPa, gamma = 26 kN/m3); single-girder A = 1.1389 m^2, I = 0.35492 m^4; combined A = 3.4168 m^2, I = 1.06475 m^4; self weight 88.84 kN/m (m = 9.056 t/m), girder self-weight only.\n- Bearings: plain laminated elastomeric 300x400 mm, 5 layers x 8 mm (te = 0.04 m), S = 10.71, 6 per abutment line (2 per girder end x 3 girders), Kv = 8.518e6 kN/m, Kh = 18000 kN/m, rotation free; both abutment lines longitudinally spring.\n- Live load: Highway Class II, 2 lanes, xi = 1.0, qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk = 240 kN per span, mu = 0.2006 from f1 = 3.402 Hz (JTG D60-2015 4.3.2).\n\nResults: first three vertical frequencies 3.402 / 13.485 / 29.876 Hz; self-weight reactions 1332.5 kN at each abutment (sum = 2665 kN, matching gamma*A*L); self-weight midspan moment 9994 kN.m; live-load max positive moment 6449.6 kN.m."
